# v060 bounded numerical method

The numerical plan freezes five ratio states from 0.99000 to 0.99100 before numerical workers. The fixed state is A=0, B=-0.4, T=-0.8, phi=80 degrees, theta=1.05 degrees, eps=0.003, w_kappa=0, w_mode=average. Both engines explicitly use lab_nn_full; their linear/exact reciprocal geometry and cutoff tolerances remain distinct. Two one-thread workers run N8; the v055 Hamiltonian adapters and guarded eight-band sampler are imported by frozen hash. No legacy Euler/braid acceptance entry point is invoked.

Six roots are continued by bounded least squares in the explicit unwrapped chart [0,1] x [0,1.1]. The node above f2=1 is preserved. Every final optimizer must succeed, have finite coordinates/residual, residual and gap below 1e-6 meV, and chart margin above .005. Root jumps must stay below .035 and same-index roots remain separated by .003. U1/U2 select the upper gap (index 4); X1..X4 select the next gap (index 5). These six seeded roots do not constitute a complete node search.

A fixed real reciprocal basis is used at every state. Polar Procrustes carries the two U frames separately along ratio. Fine ratio step .00025 and coarse step .0005 are compared at steps 2 and 4; determinants exceed .99 and subspace overlaps exceed .1. Individual temporal charge is constant. The spatial comparison is a separately transported U1-to-U2 frame. Its orientation relative to the temporally carried U2 frame may change sign; this does not flip U2's individually carried charge.

Spatial transport uses 128/256 base steps plus projected adjacent-node seeds. Both exterior gaps are sampled. Every sampled local minimum is refined by bounded scalar minimization; final success, finite values, bracket membership, nonworsening and gap >1e-5 meV are required. Additional geometric subdivisions near located minima use a conservative affine-Hamiltonian variation scale. This is numerical resolution support, not a rigorous global lower bound. Every transport point separately passes the selected-band isolation and overlap guards. The two spatial meshes must agree in orientation (determinant >.99).

Three loop/radius trials use radii .006, .006, .003 and meshes 64,128,128. Only the exact phase-step-resolution rejection permits retry at 256,512,512. Other failures immediately reject. Both temporal charges and the direct spatial charge of U2 are measured for each trial and must agree across meshes/radii. Direct spatial U2 charge must equal the orientation sign times its temporal charge. Retain every rejected stage.

X1's signed perpendicular offset from the U1-U2 segment is solved in the fixed [.9905,.991] ratio bracket by Brent at 1e-10 and 5e-12 tolerances. Both solves must converge, offsets be below 1e-7, and ratios agree within 1e-8. Projection must be interior to the segment. The selected group's exterior gap at the projected segment point must fall below 1e-5 meV, and frame extraction must specifically reject isolation loss. An unrelated numerical error does not count as that witness. Saved states must be SAME below and OPPOSITE above the located crossing for this declared target to pass; unexpected behavior is retained as a rejected case.

Complete JSON/frame checkpoints are committed atomically. The final reconciler checks their hashes, orthonormality and recorded overlap/orientation relationships without executing a Hamiltonian. It reconciles continuation seeds, optimizer metadata, all refinement counts, event evaluations and common-ratio comparisons. Publication additionally requires a complete actual test run bound to all current source/test/result and runtime identities. The publication freeze follows the run; the numerical freeze precedes it.

N4/N6 are retained evidence, not fresh execution. Their raw v042 records do not embed a held state or plan digest, so the state linkage is explicitly contextual through retained source. No continuous-interval proof, complete N8 sequence, infinite-cutoff guarantee, independent harness validation or physical-bilayer claim follows.
